  "topic": "Read and write Ya (ي) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Ya. Like 'y' in 'yes' or 'yellow'. Also sounds like 'ee' in 'tree'. Lips smile slightly!",
      "title": "Meet Ya!",
      "ar": "ي",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Ya"
    },
    {
      "en": "A curved bowl shape with TWO dots below — same base as Nun but with TWO dots under it. Ya makes you SMILE — 'Y' for Yes! And in Arabic, (ya) means 'O!' (calling someone)!",
      "title": "How to write Ya"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Ya says “ya”.",
      "title": "Ya with fatha",
      "ar": "يَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Ya says “ye”.",
      "title": "Ya with kasra",
      "ar": "يِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Ya says “yo”.",
      "title": "Ya with damma",
      "ar": "يُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Every day is new”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "كُلُّ يَوْمٍ جَدِيد",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Kullu Yawmin Jadid"
    }
